WEBVTT

00:10.110 --> 00:12.030
OOZORA

00:14.820 --> 00:16.530
So, today is the day.

00:16.530 --> 00:17.450
Yes!

00:17.450 --> 00:18.830
I'll catch up with you later.

00:18.830 --> 00:21.330
All right! You are our coach after all.

00:21.330 --> 00:26.330
OOZORA

00:21.700 --> 00:23.040
I'm off!

00:26.330 --> 00:29.050
Does he always do that when he goes outside?

00:29.050 --> 00:30.420
Yes, he does!

00:30.840 --> 00:33.340
I wonder if it's okay though.

00:33.720 --> 00:37.850
In order to improve his football skills,

00:37.850 --> 00:40.640
he was going to transfer to Shuutetsu Elementary
with the famous football club, right?

00:40.640 --> 00:43.850
He chose Nankatsu himself,
so it'll be okay.

00:43.850 --> 00:45.980
It looks like he even made friends there.

00:46.560 --> 00:47.560
Moreover,

00:47.560 --> 00:49.730
you'll be the one coaching him.

00:49.730 --> 00:52.740
His father was really happy about it.

01:07.130 --> 01:12.710
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

01:07.130 --> 01:12.710
<i>koronde toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

01:12.710 --> 01:17.390
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

01:12.710 --> 01:17.390
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

01:18.640 --> 01:23.310
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

01:18.640 --> 01:23.310
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

01:24.180 --> 01:31.900
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

01:24.180 --> 01:31.900
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:31.900 --> 01:37.660
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:31.900 --> 01:37.660
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:37.660 --> 01:46.410
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:37.660 --> 01:46.410
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:46.410 --> 01:51.960
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:46.410 --> 01:51.960
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:51.960 --> 01:57.880
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:51.960 --> 01:57.880
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:57.880 --> 01:59.550
<i>Run & Run!</i>

01:59.550 --> 02:06.770
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

01:59.550 --> 02:06.770
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

02:06.770 --> 02:09.770
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

02:06.770 --> 02:09.770
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

02:09.770 --> 02:14.190
<i>Leap out into an enormous dream field!</i>

02:09.770 --> 02:14.190
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

02:25.330 --> 02:29.330
<b>EPISODE 4 :
TSUBASA AND ROBERTO</b>

02:43.560 --> 02:47.020
MEDICAL DIAGNOSIS REPORT
MR. ROBERTO HONGO

02:53.650 --> 02:54.900
<i>Hey, Roberto!</i>

02:55.480 --> 02:57.780
<i>Have you brought the uniform you wore</i>

02:57.780 --> 02:58.820
<i>when you played for the Brazilian national team?</i>

02:58.820 --> 02:59.360
<i>What?</i>

02:59.360 --> 03:03.830
<i>I want to see the uniform you wore then, Roberto!</i>

03:05.370 --> 03:06.490
<i>All right.</i>

03:08.870 --> 03:10.750
<i>This is so cool!</i>

03:10.750 --> 03:12.420
<i>Number 10!</i>

03:12.420 --> 03:15.380
<i>Have a look at this, Mom!
It's the real thing!</i>

03:15.380 --> 03:17.210
<i>It looks really good.</i>

03:17.670 --> 03:19.260
<i>By the way Roberto,</i>

03:19.260 --> 03:21.680
<i>you have washed it, right?</i>

03:22.260 --> 03:24.140
<i>Of course I have!</i>

03:24.140 --> 03:25.310
<i>Roberto!</i>

03:25.850 --> 03:29.930
<i>I'll take the world on with the best Japanese team.</i>

03:29.930 --> 03:32.400
<i>Even Brazil won't stand a chance against me.</i>

03:32.810 --> 03:34.230
<i>There you go.</i>

03:33.190 --> 03:35.190
<i></i>

03:34.650 --> 03:37.480
<i>I won't ever forget those words.</i>

03:37.480 --> 03:38.440
<i>Okay!</i>

03:43.780 --> 03:45.240
"The world", he says...

03:45.240 --> 03:47.990
MEDICAL DIAGNOSIS REPORT
MR. ROBERTO HONGO

03:54.250 --> 03:58.500
<b>NANKATSU TOWN
NANKATSU ELEMENTARY SCHOOL</b>

03:54.250 --> 03:54.960
Good morning!

03:54.960 --> 03:58.500
What? Did you just say
that the football club won a match?

04:00.800 --> 04:03.050
How about you see the score with your own eyes?

04:03.640 --> 04:04.550
Wow, you are right!

04:04.550 --> 04:06.550
You won 5-2 against Nishigaoka Elementary?

04:06.550 --> 04:07.680
That's awesome!

04:07.680 --> 04:11.020
How did your lame football club
managed to score 5 goals?

04:12.480 --> 04:14.980
Well, thank you for asking.

04:14.980 --> 04:17.270
Our new club member, Oozora Tsubasa,

04:17.270 --> 04:19.940
scored four of those goals all by himself.

04:19.940 --> 04:22.820
What's more, the one who scored
the deciding fifth goal was me!

04:23.610 --> 04:27.450
My head shot made a perfect goal!

04:27.450 --> 04:30.660
It was thanks to Tsubasa's cross though.

04:30.660 --> 04:33.830
Hold on a minute. Who is this Tsubasa
you've been talking about?

04:33.830 --> 04:36.460
When did you have a new member?

04:36.460 --> 04:37.710
Well,

04:37.710 --> 04:41.840
we had a fated encounter during this spring break.

04:41.840 --> 04:44.680
Fate?
What are you talking about?

04:44.680 --> 04:47.760
So, it means that if it weren't for that Tsubasa guy,

04:47.760 --> 04:49.390
you wouldn't have scored any goal.

04:50.470 --> 04:53.730
One person scoring four goals
is even better than a hat trick.

04:53.730 --> 04:56.350
Even Shuutetsu doesn't have someone like him.

04:56.350 --> 04:58.980
We have other things that will surprise you.

04:58.980 --> 05:01.150
Our football club now has a coach.

05:01.150 --> 05:03.110
Yeah, I nearly forgot.

05:03.110 --> 05:07.660
Our coach is a former member of
the Brazilian national football team, Roberto Hongo.

05:08.030 --> 05:09.620
Brazilian national team?

05:09.620 --> 05:13.500
Isn't that awesome?
He's an acquiantance of Tsubasa.

05:13.500 --> 05:16.670
Just what kind of guy is Oozora Tsubasa?

05:16.670 --> 05:18.380
Look, Tsubasa is coming.

05:23.510 --> 05:24.970
Is that Tsubasa?

05:24.970 --> 05:27.510
Yeah, that's Oozora Tsubasa.

05:27.510 --> 05:30.140
Why is he dribbling?

05:30.140 --> 05:33.270
As expected of him. He's probably
been dribbling his way from home.

05:33.270 --> 05:34.480
From his home?

05:34.480 --> 05:36.310
He's always like that.

05:36.310 --> 05:38.980
Wherever he goes, he keeps on dribbling.

05:38.980 --> 05:40.270
Is that so?

05:40.270 --> 05:41.650
He's really good at it.

05:41.650 --> 05:44.900
It must be true that he scored five goals.

05:44.900 --> 05:47.030
He looks like the kind of guy who can do it.

05:47.030 --> 05:48.910
Well, I scored one of them.

05:48.910 --> 05:51.030
He only got four goals in.

05:51.030 --> 05:54.040
Hey, Tsubasa!

05:54.040 --> 05:56.500
Good morning, Ishizaki!

05:58.040 --> 06:01.040
6TH YEAR CLASS 1

06:01.040 --> 06:05.380
<i>OOZORA TSUBASA</i>

06:05.380 --> 06:08.720
This is Oozora Tsubasa,

06:08.720 --> 06:10.600
he'll be your friend from today on.

06:10.600 --> 06:12.760
Get on well with him, everyone.

06:12.760 --> 06:16.430
My name is Oozora Tsubasa.
Nice to meet you!

06:17.480 --> 06:19.020
By the way,

06:19.560 --> 06:23.570
why have you brought a football here?

06:23.570 --> 06:25.110
It's my friend.

06:25.110 --> 06:27.400
Your friend?

06:27.400 --> 06:28.320
Yes!

06:28.320 --> 06:32.030
Teacher,
Tsubasa has joined the football club.

06:32.030 --> 06:34.910
This year, our club will be different from before.

06:34.910 --> 06:37.120
The inter-school tournament will be great!

06:37.120 --> 06:40.460
Cheer leader,
I'm trusting you with cheering us on.

06:40.460 --> 06:43.380
Will you be okay with setting your goals that high?

06:43.380 --> 06:45.420
Isn't Tsubasa the awesome one?

06:45.420 --> 06:48.340
The rest of you are just members of the no-good football club.

06:48.340 --> 06:49.880
That's not true.

06:51.680 --> 06:53.260
Until the tournament,
if Ishizaki and the others become

06:53.260 --> 06:56.390
even better friends with the ball,
they'll get better at football.

06:56.390 --> 06:59.940
Roberto said so.

06:59.940 --> 07:02.150
He said it again, "friend".

07:02.150 --> 07:03.310
Very well!

07:03.310 --> 07:07.190
Let's go and see the football club's practice after school.

07:07.190 --> 07:08.240
All right!

07:09.360 --> 07:10.990
Well,

07:10.990 --> 07:14.280
the entrance ceremony is about to begin.

07:15.370 --> 07:17.790
<i>Students of Nankatsu Elementary,</i>

07:17.790 --> 07:22.290
<i>especially those in the fourth and
upper grades who are in a sports club,</i>

07:22.290 --> 07:26.590
<i>are all restlessly waiting for
today's entrance ceremony to end.</i>

07:27.300 --> 07:30.090
<i>From today on,</i>

07:30.090 --> 07:33.470
<i>you'll start intensely practicing in preperation
for the inter-school tournament with Shuutetsu.</i>

07:34.430 --> 07:36.850
- Don't slack off!
- Okay!

07:36.850 --> 07:41.100
This year's inter-school tournament has
baseball club's third year of consecutive victories at stake!

07:41.100 --> 07:42.770
Yeah!

07:42.770 --> 07:44.900
We, the kendo club,

07:45.230 --> 07:48.030
will erase last year's humiliation!

07:48.440 --> 07:50.320
Don't give up, keep on running!

07:50.320 --> 07:53.660
The inter-school tournament is just around the corner.
Don't relax yet!

07:54.570 --> 07:55.990
<i>The inter-school tournament...</i>

07:56.450 --> 07:59.330
<i>It's a sports festival where each club of
the two elementary schools of this town,</i>

07:59.330 --> 08:02.330
<i>Nankatsu Elementary and Shuutetsu Elementary,</i>

08:02.330 --> 08:06.840
<i>compete during a whole day.</i>

08:06.840 --> 08:09.170
<i>On the eve of the 26th tournament,</i>

08:08.250 --> 08:14.300
<b>SHUUTETSU                                  NANKATSU</b>

08:09.170 --> 08:12.720
<i>Nankatsu has 12 victories,
12 losses and a draw.</i>

08:12.720 --> 08:14.470
<i>It's a perfect tie.</i>

08:13.300 --> 08:15.010
<b>12 WINS 12 LOSSES 1 DRAW</b>

08:15.430 --> 08:16.600
NANKATSU'S CERTAIN VICTORY

08:16.600 --> 08:19.100
One, two! One, two!

08:19.100 --> 08:21.940
This year, we'll finally settle the score.

08:21.940 --> 08:24.520
It's no wonder that each club is fired up.

08:24.520 --> 08:25.980
Right, Boss?

08:26.860 --> 08:29.230
The biggest problem is the football club.

08:29.230 --> 08:32.780
Let's go and see how good Tsubasa is, Boss!

08:32.780 --> 08:35.450
All right, we're off to the football field!

08:35.450 --> 08:36.780
Okay!

08:41.750 --> 08:45.330
Oh my, Roberto just left this lying around here.

08:45.880 --> 08:51.090
Ace striker, number 10...
Roberto Hongo.

08:51.380 --> 08:55.090
He's not Tsubasa, but that's still very cool.

08:55.090 --> 08:57.550
Oh, I need to clean.

09:01.600 --> 09:02.850
Oh no!

09:05.560 --> 09:09.570
MEDICAL DIAGNOSIS REPORT
MR. ROBERTO HONGO

09:07.730 --> 09:09.570
"Ophthalmology"?

09:11.650 --> 09:13.190
I'm sorry, Roberto.

09:21.040 --> 09:22.410
What does this mean?

09:26.580 --> 09:28.130
Roberto...

09:28.130 --> 09:29.380
It can't be...{part two-burcu}

09:52.940 --> 09:54.780
The weather's so nice!

09:58.530 --> 10:00.950
<i>Dear Coach João,</i>

10:01.950 --> 10:03.450
<i>After all, it was useless.</i>

10:04.200 --> 10:05.960
<i>I did verything I could,</i>

10:05.960 --> 10:07.790
<i>and upon the advice of Captain Oozora,</i>

10:07.790 --> 10:10.420
<i>I've finally made it back to Japan.</i>

10:11.420 --> 10:13.960
<i>Yet, the diagnosis results still say that</i>

10:13.960 --> 10:15.470
<i>I have retinal detachment.</i>

10:16.090 --> 10:18.300
<i>It's true that we were late to notice it.</i>

10:18.300 --> 10:20.720
<i>If I keep on playing football any longer,</i>

10:24.100 --> 10:27.310
<i>and receive a strong shock during a match,</i>

10:28.190 --> 10:32.110
<i>I will become blind forever. </i>

10:34.690 --> 10:37.740
<i>Please announce that I'll be retiring.</i>

10:37.740 --> 10:40.990
<i>I plan to stay in Japan for the time being.</i>

10:42.240 --> 10:46.160
Incredible dribbles from the Brazilian
national team player, Roberto Hongo! !

10:47.290 --> 10:50.580
<i>No, I have become unable to play football.</i>

10:51.040 --> 10:55.090
<i>As things are, it might be best for me
if I lived in my homeland, Japan.</i>

10:56.170 --> 10:58.090
<i>You don't need to worry about me.</i>

10:59.470 --> 11:04.140
<i>I've been preparing myself for this
ever since I left Brazil.</i>

11:08.560 --> 11:12.400
<i>But if ever return to Brazil one day,</i>

11:12.400 --> 11:13.360
<i>I have a feeling that</i>

11:13.860 --> 11:16.400
<i>I won't be alone.</i>

11:17.900 --> 11:21.530
<i>In my homeland, Japan, I've found a new flame.</i>

11:21.530 --> 11:23.740
Guys, let's start practicing!

11:23.740 --> 11:24.870
Yeah!

11:24.870 --> 11:28.290
<i>And that flame's name is Oozora Tsubasa.</i>

11:29.120 --> 11:31.620
- Roberto!
- Coach!

11:33.790 --> 11:35.210
All right! Let's do this!

11:36.670 --> 11:37.880
Roberto!

11:46.510 --> 11:48.890
Awe-awesome...

11:50.190 --> 11:52.190
Nice shot, Roberto!

11:52.190 --> 11:54.110
Nice pass, Tsubasa!

11:55.730 --> 11:56.940
Cool!

11:56.940 --> 11:59.240
Did you see it? Did you?
Did you see what happened now?

11:59.240 --> 12:01.070
Yeah...

12:01.070 --> 12:02.780
Tsubasa is cool too,

12:02.780 --> 12:06.200
but that old man is not bad either.
That long shoot was something.

12:06.200 --> 12:08.040
Is that their coach?

12:08.040 --> 12:11.460
You know, the one Ishizaki was
talking about, the Brazilian player.

12:11.460 --> 12:14.170
He was called "something" Hongo.

12:14.630 --> 12:16.340
The name's Roberto Hongo.

12:16.340 --> 12:19.130
You are talking to
a Brazilian national player, guys.

12:19.130 --> 12:20.880
An ex-player though.

12:21.340 --> 12:22.840
Who are you?

12:22.840 --> 12:25.010
They are the cheering squad of Nankatsu.

12:26.180 --> 12:27.970
My name is Nakazawa Sanae.

12:27.970 --> 12:30.560
I'm the leader of Nankatsu Elementary's cheering squad.

12:30.560 --> 12:32.060
Everyone calls her "Boss".

12:32.060 --> 12:34.190
You didn't have to say that now.

12:35.440 --> 12:38.690
Really? Have you come to cheer our football club?

12:38.690 --> 12:39.650
Well, not really.

12:39.650 --> 12:42.860
We heard about yesterday's match with
Nishigaoka Elementary from Ishizaki,

12:42.860 --> 12:46.620
and we've become curious about Tsubasa and you, coach.

12:47.620 --> 12:50.200
Ishizaki was boasting about

12:50.200 --> 12:52.500
our lame football club having such a big transformation.

12:52.500 --> 12:54.920
We've come to see how you have changed.

12:58.880 --> 13:02.630
Okay! We'll start with a match.

13:02.630 --> 13:03.840
A match?

13:03.840 --> 13:07.100
It's a welcoming party for our new member, Tsubasa.

13:15.480 --> 13:18.110
Is this a welcoming party?

13:18.110 --> 13:20.570
This will be the opposite of the time
when I first met Tsubasa,

13:20.570 --> 13:23.860
the match between him and B team of Shuutetsu.

13:24.240 --> 13:26.490
Tsubasa will be attacking alone.

13:26.490 --> 13:29.870
Ishizaki and others will pass the ball, mark him...

13:29.870 --> 13:33.040
In short, you'll try not to have the ball taken from you.

13:33.410 --> 13:35.670
If Tsubasa gets the ball, he'll shoot.

13:35.670 --> 13:37.880
The time limit is five minutes.

13:37.880 --> 13:40.460
If his shoot becomes a goal, Tsubasa wins.

13:40.460 --> 13:44.260
If you manage to protect your goal
for five minutes, Ishizaki's side wins.

13:44.260 --> 13:45.380
Okay!

13:45.380 --> 13:47.470
Isn't this a crazy game?

13:47.470 --> 13:50.260
Even if it's Tsubasa, isn't being alone hard?

13:50.260 --> 13:52.640
Sshh! Shut up and watch.

13:54.640 --> 13:57.100
We are playing against Tsubasa...

13:57.100 --> 13:59.270
He'll get the ball in the blink of an eye.

13:59.270 --> 14:01.770
You guys are too weak!

14:01.770 --> 14:04.150
If he takes the ball,
you just have to take it back.

14:04.150 --> 14:06.280
Wouldn't winning against Tsubasa be the best?

14:06.570 --> 14:08.570
Ishizaki, you are so optimistic!

14:08.570 --> 14:12.120
Us vs. Tsubasa... Let's do this!

14:12.870 --> 14:14.910
Come, Tsubasa!

14:14.910 --> 14:16.920
Here I go, everyone!

14:24.880 --> 14:26.260
Start!

14:27.380 --> 14:30.640
Here he comes! Nagano, follow Tsubasa!

14:30.640 --> 14:31.640
I'm on it!

14:35.140 --> 14:37.020
I'm sorry Tsubasa.

14:37.020 --> 14:39.650
We'll be holding you down for the next five minutes.

14:44.110 --> 14:45.570
He's passed!

14:45.570 --> 14:47.820
Hey, he's wide open.

14:47.820 --> 14:49.240
Oda!

14:53.030 --> 14:55.040
Nakazato!

14:57.160 --> 14:58.120
Oh shit!

14:58.120 --> 14:59.790
God damn it!

15:01.750 --> 15:03.750
Come on, recover it!

15:03.750 --> 15:05.420
I've got it.

15:08.260 --> 15:09.630
He's fast.

15:13.850 --> 15:15.810
Guys, chase him!

15:23.360 --> 15:24.570
He's so strong.

15:24.570 --> 15:27.320
Ishizaki's team is no match for him.

15:27.320 --> 15:29.740
He's got great talent, Boss.

15:29.740 --> 15:32.570
It's like the ball is a part of him.

15:34.580 --> 15:36.330
3 minutes to go.

15:36.330 --> 15:38.290
We still have time.

15:38.290 --> 15:40.540
Let's recover the ball.

15:40.540 --> 15:42.880
We must not disappoint Roberto!

15:42.880 --> 15:44.880
- Ok!
- All right!

15:51.470 --> 15:53.340
Get up, Manabu.

15:53.340 --> 15:55.100
Just one more minute left.

16:01.600 --> 16:02.440
<i>Good!</i>

16:03.100 --> 16:05.190
<i>They've changed their attitude!</i>

16:05.650 --> 16:09.690
<i>We'll quickly improve ourselves
by training with Tsubasa!</i>

16:10.150 --> 16:14.700
<i>Coach knew about that,
that's why he chose him as our opponent!</i>

16:14.700 --> 16:19.080
<i>Perfect, we'll go for the victory
in the inter-school tournament!</i>

16:27.090 --> 16:28.960
Let's go!

16:33.550 --> 16:35.550
It's in the back of the net!

16:36.300 --> 16:37.810
It's over!

16:49.940 --> 16:52.570
Too bad, we've lost it!

16:52.570 --> 16:55.820
Tsubasa is really amazing!

16:55.820 --> 16:59.580
Tsubasa, you always have a hell of a kick.

16:59.580 --> 17:01.960
It's because of my love for the football.

17:05.540 --> 17:07.960
What the hell is wrong with you, Boss?

17:07.960 --> 17:09.800
Have you lost your tongue?

17:09.800 --> 17:11.760
You look like a different person.

17:11.760 --> 17:13.510
Boss? Hello?

17:14.840 --> 17:16.090
Tsubasa...

17:17.890 --> 17:19.760
is so cool!

17:21.100 --> 17:23.890
You're getting mushy!

17:23.890 --> 17:25.650
Congratulations to everyone.

17:26.060 --> 17:29.400
You have managed to cling to Tsubasa.

17:29.400 --> 17:32.400
Now you're going to follow my methods exactly.

17:32.400 --> 17:34.070
- Cool?
- Yes.

17:42.250 --> 17:43.040
Shoot!

17:58.930 --> 18:00.720
Is there any news?

18:00.720 --> 18:03.850
Yes, they've started seriously training

18:03.850 --> 18:06.520
under the direction of Roberto Hongo.

18:06.850 --> 18:11.520
I'm curious to see how far that team will progress

18:11.520 --> 18:12.940
under his direction.

18:13.440 --> 18:15.990
Other players are worthless.

18:17.700 --> 18:22.040
Against Nishigaoka only Tsubasa made the difference.

18:22.490 --> 18:24.410
Don't underestimate them.

18:25.870 --> 18:29.630
Sure, but only Tsubasa can match me.

18:34.840 --> 18:37.760
That training was really hard.

18:37.760 --> 18:41.140
This Brazilian coach gave them a hard time.

18:41.140 --> 18:43.510
I'm exhausted just by looking at them.

18:43.510 --> 18:45.390
I'm toasted!

18:45.390 --> 18:47.480
And I can't move.

18:47.480 --> 18:50.610
Seriously, you guys are bunch of sissies.

18:50.610 --> 18:52.570
What the hell is your problem, Boss?

18:52.570 --> 18:54.030
Look at Tsubasa.

18:54.030 --> 18:56.570
He still looks good.

18:56.570 --> 18:59.530
Bu he's not like us!

18:59.530 --> 19:03.030
No wonder everybody calls you lame.

19:03.030 --> 19:05.290
I thought you guys had changed?

19:05.290 --> 19:08.580
Calm down. It'll take time.

19:08.580 --> 19:09.790
Be patient.

19:09.790 --> 19:11.500
But, I can't!

19:11.500 --> 19:13.710
Inter-school tournament is about to start!

19:13.710 --> 19:16.550
You're right!
That's why,

19:16.550 --> 19:18.420
you'll have to be friends with the ball

19:18.420 --> 19:21.340
to win your match.

19:21.340 --> 19:25.220
Tsubasa and coach
often talk about that.

19:25.220 --> 19:27.520
How can we become friends with the ball?

19:27.520 --> 19:29.850
Always be with it.

19:29.850 --> 19:32.730
Take it everywhere where you're going,

19:32.730 --> 19:35.730
at school, while eating lunch etc.

19:36.530 --> 19:39.650
Isn't that how always you do, Tsubasa?

19:39.650 --> 19:41.030
Yeah, pretty much.

19:41.030 --> 19:44.030
Are you dribbling all the way coming to school?

19:44.030 --> 19:45.290
Yes!

19:45.290 --> 19:49.040
Tsubasa didn't learn that from me.

19:49.040 --> 19:51.790
He's been doing it since he was a little boy.

19:53.000 --> 19:55.920
From now on, you can't use your hands.

19:55.920 --> 19:59.340
The football doesn't like to be carried on hands.

19:59.340 --> 20:00.880
No way!

20:00.880 --> 20:02.470
Do we have to dribble

20:02.470 --> 20:05.470
wherever we go like Tsubasa?

20:05.850 --> 20:07.470
You can do it!

20:07.470 --> 20:09.180
Yeah, you have to!

20:09.180 --> 20:10.850
Easy for you to say.

20:10.850 --> 20:12.480
You want to get better, right?

20:12.480 --> 20:15.020
What about the goalkeepers?

20:15.020 --> 20:17.980
Same goes for you but sometimes

20:18.360 --> 20:20.240
you can use your hands too.

20:20.240 --> 20:22.780
- Cool!
- That's not fair!

20:22.780 --> 20:24.910
That will be all for today.

20:24.910 --> 20:27.540
Go home while dribbling!

20:27.540 --> 20:30.660
W-What?

20:30.660 --> 20:32.920
See you later Tsubasa.

20:32.920 --> 20:35.420
See you tomorrow guys.

20:35.420 --> 20:37.750
Be careful.

20:37.750 --> 20:40.010
Don't be an embarrassment to Tsubasa!

20:40.010 --> 20:41.510
Shut up!

20:42.430 --> 20:44.510
It seems like very hard for them.

20:44.510 --> 20:46.430
These guys are awful...

20:46.430 --> 20:49.180
That's how they will make a progress.

20:50.980 --> 20:52.690
Can't wait for

20:52.690 --> 20:54.730
the start of the inter-school tournament!

20:57.400 --> 21:00.990
I'm starving!
I have to go home quickly.

21:02.740 --> 21:05.620
What am I going to do Ishizaki?

21:05.620 --> 21:07.450
What a mess...

21:07.450 --> 21:08.240
Huh?

21:08.240 --> 21:11.000
Do you live around here Manabu?

21:11.000 --> 21:15.000
Not really
but my friend won't listen to me!

21:15.000 --> 21:19.050
I'm not sure if we can make it home like this.

21:19.050 --> 21:21.260
It's cool to be goalkeeper!

21:26.890 --> 21:28.430
<i>He's very good.</i>

21:28.430 --> 21:30.680
<i>As good as when I was at his age.</i>

21:31.100 --> 21:34.270
<i>No... maybe even more.</i>

21:36.690 --> 21:40.070
There you go!
The ball hasn't touched the ground.

21:40.070 --> 21:42.440
Do you like football Tsubasa?

21:42.440 --> 21:45.150
What a question, of course I do!

21:45.570 --> 21:49.410
Perfect!
From now on you have to wake up at 5 AM to train.

21:49.830 --> 21:53.750
I'll teach you what real Brazilian football is.

21:54.370 --> 21:55.160
All right.

21:57.920 --> 21:59.420
<i>Dear coach João,</i>

21:59.420 --> 22:03.050
<i>I've found a glimmer of light.</i>

22:03.920 --> 22:05.970
<i>His name is Oozora Tsubasa.</i>

22:06.890 --> 22:09.010
<i>I'll take my chances on him.</i>

22:09.010 --> 22:12.890
<i>I'll make him a world-renowned player.</i>

22:13.770 --> 22:15.230
<i>I've left the pitch,</i>

22:15.230 --> 22:18.230
<i>but football will always be a part of my life.</i>

22:38.960 --> 22:44.840
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.960 --> 22:44.840
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.850
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.840 --> 22:50.850
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.850 --> 22:56.850
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.850 --> 22:56.850
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:02.980
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:02.980
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:02.980 --> 23:09.070
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:02.980 --> 23:09.070
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.070 --> 23:15.160
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.070 --> 23:15.160
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.160 --> 23:21.210
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.210 --> 23:26.210
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.210 --> 23:26.210
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.670 --> 23:33.390
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.670 --> 23:33.390
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.390 --> 23:39.270
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.270 --> 23:45.820
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.270 --> 23:45.820
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.740 --> 23:58.870
COMING UP, EPISODE 5 :

23:49.740 --> 23:58.870
ON THEIR WAY TO THE INTER-SCHOOL TOURNAMENT
